From f874e5df9e115c08c96c08888057a093b8c4a092 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:07:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Matchmaker: public read-only GET /status with cabinet totals

GET /status returns {"service","version","online","searching","inMatch",
"matches","updatedAt","cacheSeconds"} for launchers (player count + ping).
Totals only: no card ids, access codes, chip ids, names, serials, node ids
or IP addresses. Cabinets are counted by pcb serial + public IP; searching =
in the queue now, inMatch = placed in a room within InMatchWindowSeconds and
not searching again, online = seen within OnlineWindowSeconds.

Security: under PublicMatchmaker the internet may reach exactly /status
(not sub-paths, which would hit the WebUI fallback); own per-IP token bucket
(Status.RequestsPerMinute / Burst) and a CacheSeconds reply cache.
Status.PublicStatus=false answers 404. Defaults apply without config.

Tests: Matchmaking.Tests +15 (472/472).

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
